oney.py` said it used banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so `2.665` now rounds to `2.66` and `2.675` to `2.68`, which is what `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n\n**Steps:**\n- I made the change on a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, and the first CI run passed.\n- The first attempt to open the PR was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into it, checked the fix was still there and ran CI again. That run passed too, and then the PR opened.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}